This export carries none of the four axes — every one of the 12000 transactions abstains on version, input order, locktime and fee rate — so the vectors compared here are structural: degree, transaction count, self-transfers and the neighbour-degree histogram. On those alone the space is dense, and markedly less so among the higher-degree vertices (0.876 against 0.998 at the same threshold), which is where a matcher would start. The contracted graph is disassortative. These observations do not reproduce the historical larger slices, do not measure attribute density, and do not establish graph-matching performance.
